{"name":"Rising Star","hex":"#f7f6d5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rising star","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An emerging talent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rising_star"}],"entries":[{"title":"Armin van Buuren","blocks":[{"text":"Armin Jozef Jacobus Daniël van Buuren OON is a Dutch DJ, musician and record producer. Since 2001, he has hosted A State of Trance (ASOT), a weekly radio show, which is broadcast to nearly 40 million listeners in 84 countries on over 100 FM radio stations. According to the website DJs and Festivals, \"the radio show propelled him to stardom and helped cultivate an interest in trance music around the world\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Armin_van_Buuren%2C_November_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Armin_van_Buuren%2C_November_2025_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Armin_van_Buuren"},{"title":"Aurvandill","blocks":[{"text":"Aurvandill is a figure in Germanic mythology. In Norse mythology, the god Thor tosses Aurvandill's toe – which had frozen while the thunder god was carrying him in a basket across the Élivágar rivers – into the sky to form a star called Aurvandils-tá. In wider medieval Germanic-speaking cultures, he was known as Ēarendel in Old English, Aurendil in Old High German, Auriwandalo in Lombardic, and possibly as auzandil (𐌰𐌿𐌶𐌰𐌽𐌳𐌹𐌻) in Gothic. An Old Danish latinized version, Horwendillus (Ørvendil), is also the name given to the father of Amlethus (Amleth) in Saxo Grammaticus' Gesta Danorum."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Hardvendels_Kamp_med_Koll.jpg/330px-Hardvendels_Kamp_med_Koll.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurvandill"},{"title":"Rising Star (Israeli TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"HaKokhav HaBa is an Israeli interactive reality singing competition, created by Keshet Media Group and broadcast on Channel 2 and on Channel 12. It is the basis of the Rising Star franchise. The show is a continuation of Kokhav Nolad which featured aspiring singers competing for a winning title. The program's format combines the internet, smartphone and television and is filmed live. Between 2015 and 2020, and since 2024, the show has been used to select Israel's representative for the Eurovision Song Contest."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/RisingStarIsrael.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rising_Star_(Israeli_TV_series)"},{"title":"Star","blocks":[{"text":"A star is a luminous spheroid of plasma held together by self-gravity. The nearest star to Earth is the Sun. Many other stars are visible to the naked eye at night; their immense distances from Earth make them appear as fixed points of light. The most prominent stars have been categorised into constellations and asterisms, and many of the brightest stars have proper names. Astronomers have assembled star catalogues that identify the known stars and provide standardized stellar designations. The observable universe contains an estimated 1022 to 1024 stars. Only about 4,000 of these stars are visible to the naked eye—all within the Milky Way galaxy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg/330px-The_Sun_in_white_light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Star"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Armin_van_Buuren_2005_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Armin_van_Buuren_2005_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Armin_van_Buuren_2005_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Armin_van_Buuren_2005_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Armin van Buuren at Sensation White 2005","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArmin_van_Buuren_2005_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Armin_on_air.jpg/500px-Armin_on_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Armin_on_air.jpg/1280px-Armin_on_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Armin_on_air.jpg/500px-Armin_on_air.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Van Buuren broadcasting the milestone 500th episode of his A State of Trance show at the official pre-party, live from Club Trinity in Cape Town on 17 March 2011","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArmin_on_air.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Starsinthesky.jpg/500px-Starsinthesky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Starsinthesky.jpg/1280px-Starsinthesky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/62/Starsinthesky.jpg/500px-Starsinthesky.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStarsinthesky.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Dibuix_de_Leo.png/330px-Dibuix_de_Leo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0f/Dibuix_de_Leo.png/330px-Dibuix_de_Leo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 1690 depiction of the con